<article class="env-lemma" id="07DY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07DY">Lemma <span data-tag="07DY">10.128.2</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. Assume that $R$ is a regular local ring and that a regular system of parameters maps to a regular sequence in $S$. Then $R \to S$ is flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $x_1, \ldots , x_ d$ are a system of parameters of $R$ which map to a regular sequence in $S$. Note that $S/(x_1, \ldots , x_ d)S$ is flat over $R/(x_1, \ldots , x_ d)$ as the latter is a field. Then $x_ d$ is a nonzerodivisor in $S/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 1})S$ hence $S/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 1})S$ is flat over $R/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 1})$ by the local criterion of flatness (see Lemma <a href="/tag/00ML" data-tag="00ML">10.99.10</a> and remarks following). Then $x_{d - 1}$ is a nonzerodivisor in $S/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 2})S$ hence $S/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 2})S$ is flat over $R/(x_1, \ldots , x_{d - 2})$ by the local criterion of flatness (see Lemma <a href="/tag/00ML" data-tag="00ML">10.99.10</a> and remarks following). Continue till one reaches the conclusion that $S$ is flat over $R$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>